<ContentLayout title="The Kryos Ecosystem" description="Kryos is an independent computing ecosystem centered on Kryos OS, with Veckt as its browser." heading="One ecosystem. One direction." lead="Kryos brings its operating system, browser and supporting software under one coherent direction. Kryos OS is the foundation; Veckt is the browser workstream.">
  <section class="section shell">
    <article class="ecosystem-feature">
      <div><h2>Kryos OS</h2><p class="content-copy">The foundation of the ecosystem. A from-scratch operating-system project written in Rust, following a capability-based microkernel architecture. It remains in development; release status is published separately.</p><a class="text-link" href="/en/ecosystem/os/">Explore Kryos OS ↗</a></div>
    </article>
    <article class="ecosystem-feature ecosystem-feature-secondary">
      <div><h2>Veckt Browser</h2><p class="content-copy">The web browser within the Kryos ecosystem. Veckt is developed as a companion application, with its own implementation, security boundaries and release requirements.</p><a class="text-link" href="/en/ecosystem/browser/">Explore Veckt ↗</a></div>
    </article>
    <div class="ecosystem-note"><h2>One project. Connected components.</h2><p class="content-copy">Kryos is the ecosystem. Kryos OS and Veckt are its products; the website is the public home for the project, not another product.</p></div>
  </section>
</ContentLayout>